Stashes... mmm. It's always wise to not to store every
egg in the same nest. 
Sokoban is indeed a great early-game stash place.

And Fort Ludios...
I'm not usually this paranoid, but what if a player
made a stash on top of the _portal_ to the dungeons
of doom (on the Ludios side) ? 
A gelatinous cube, going from Dungeons to Ludios
would end up on the stash, right ? But what would
happen if the player followed the cube - would the player
displace the cube or the other way around ?

Guest is pretty good place too, because you'll know
what kinds of monsters will be generated there. Again,
near a portal might be nice, so you can get to your stash
before anything else can.

I usually stash lots of stuff just near the portal to Dungeons.

The ultimate stash would be, I guess, bury it in a pit (or water---
not for paper etc., of course) with a boulder, and place another
boulder on top of it. This works every time you have a pick-axe
and a kazillion boulders. Now only ie. a giant with a /oDigging would
ruin the stash.

